course: dictionary
lesson: 9126
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Smudge can be a thing (a noun) or an action (a verb). Context, the words around it, tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «The Andromeda Galaxy is a faint smudge in autumn skies.» Here a smudge is a blurred patch of light, not a dirty mark. The clues are faint and farthest thing most people can see with the naked eye: it is hard to see clearly.
explain: When you rub ink or chalk with your finger, you smudge it. «My writing smudged» means it became blurred and messy. Artists smudge charcoal on purpose to make soft shading. Always check: does your meaning fit the sentence?
fact: Smudge can be a noun (a smudge) or a verb (to smudge).
fact: «Smudge» as a noun means a dirty or blurred mark, like a smear of ink, paint or chocolate.
fact: «Smudge» as a verb means to make something blurred or messy by rubbing it, or to become blurred.
fact: In art, to smudge means to blend chalk, charcoal or pastel on purpose with your finger to make soft shading.
fact: «Smudge-proof» means a thing that does not smudge.
exercise: «The Andromeda Galaxy is a faint smudge in autumn skies.» What is a smudge here? | A dirty mark on a page | A kind of sweet | *A blurred, faint patch of light | A loud noise in the sky
exercise: Left-handed Sam's ink «smudged across the page». What does smudged mean? | Shone brightly | Dried very quickly | Was torn into pieces | *Became blurred and messy
exercise: In art class, Mia uses her finger to smudge the charcoal. What does smudge mean here? | *To blend charcoal on purpose to make soft shading | To sign her name | To draw a sharp, straight line | To wipe the whole picture off the paper
test: «The cake left a chocolate smudge on her cheek.» What is the smudge? | A kind of hat | A loud sound | *A dirty or blurred mark | A small cake
test: «Please do not smudge your work.» What does smudge mean here? | To hang it on the wall | *To make it blurred or messy by rubbing | To make it shine | To finish it quickly
exam: In «The smudge stayed on the page», what kind of word is smudge? | *A noun | A joke | A place name | A verb
